 "english": {
  "elements": [
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "Upon Anna's head, fragrant with the scent of wisdom,",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "thinking gold itself would hurt him,",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "they placed a crown of flowers.",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "Softer than the softness of flower petals,",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "a sacred heart — a loving heart —",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "Anna's embracing heart — his",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "flower-petals speak Tamil —",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "mango, jackfruit, banana—the three fruits. Even they would be defeated!",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "The flowers of his eyes become spears — become swords",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "if any harm should come to Mother Tamil!",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "Though the flowers of his feet may wither — his",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "arduous journey will not stop!",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "The flowers of his hands hold together the younger brothers—the Kazhagam!",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "Those very flowers forgive enemies",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "and make their heads bow like ripened ears of paddy.",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "As democracy's flower sways,",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "as the flower of social equality spreads fragrance,",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "with Tamil, the mother tongue, as life's garden,",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "O flower crown sought by the dancing breeze! O crown of fame! Among",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "the heaps of greetings that seek you, each day",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "I shall fly as a bee that comes singing...",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "To guard you, I shall give myself up.",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   },
   {
    "kind": "stanza-break",
    "evidence": "source-blank-line",
    "sourceScan": 4
   },
   {
    "kind": "line",
    "text": "M. Karunanidhi",
    "indent": 0,
    "sourceScan": 4,
    "printedPage": null
   }
  ],
